        "topic": "Double-Entry Rules",
        "question_type": "Objective",
        "exam_year": "2015",
        "question_text": "<p>In double-entry bookkeeping, which of the following accounts is credited when cash is received from a debtor?</p>",
        "question_image": null,
        "answer_image": null,
        "explanation": "<p>When cash is received from a debtor, the cash account (an asset) increases and is debited, while the debtor's account (also an asset) decreases and is credited. This follows the rule that for every debit, there must be an equal and opposite credit.</p>",
        "reference_passage": null,
        "novel": null,
        "comments_count": 0,
        "options": [
